- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.StudyEngineTests`

**How to implement.** The study engine solves from the parameters' own starts within their own bounds (the S11.3 brief 'The start is the parameters' start values, the bounds come from their states'), while the S10.1 fit wrapper `MuellerFitting.fitWithResidual` (step 337) always starts at the zero scaled vector inside a symmetric box. The solve request moves into one member both call (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call'; AGENTS.md 'Reuse, never copy'), so one request (`IterationCount 400`, `StepTolerance 1.0e-12`, the ALGLIB Levenberg–Marquardt proxy) exists. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S11.3. In `OpticalConstructor.Optimization/MuellerFitting.fs`, after `SearchBox` (step 337): (1) `ScaledSearch = { start : ScaledVector; lowerBounds : ScaledVector; upperBounds : ScaledVector }` (`MuellerInverse.fs:ScaledVector`, a `NumericCarrier`), where a scaled solve starts and the box it keeps to. (2) `type ScaledSearch with member this.solveWith (watch : IterationWatch) (residual : ScaledVector -> ResidualVector) : Result<NonlinearSolution, NonlinearSolverError>`: the `NonlinearRequest` (`MuellerInverse.fs:NonlinearRequest`) `{ residual; initial = this.start; lowerBounds = this.lowerBounds; upperBounds = this.upperBounds; maxIterations = IterationCount 400; epsX = StepTolerance 1.0e-12 }` through `watch.levenbergMarquardtSolver` (step 380). (3) On `SearchBox`, `member this.centredSearch (dimension : int) : ScaledSearch`: the zero start and bounds of minus and plus `halfWidth` in every coordinate, `fitWithResidual`'s box today. (4) `fitWithResidual` becomes `(box.centredSearch scaling.dimension).solveWith UnwatchedIterations residual`, its `Ok` mapped to the same `MuellerFitData` record and its `Error e` to `NonlinearFitErr e` as today; the request and its numbers are unchanged, so every BerremanTests number is bit-identical. No other member, scaling or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/StudyEngineTests.fs`, `module StudyEngineTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended at the end of `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list with no comment, the home of the study engine's facts: `a scaled search starts where it is told and keeps to its own box`: the residual r(v) = [v0 − 5] from start [0.5] within [−1; 2] answers a solution of 2 (pinned at its upper bound) and within [−10; 10] a solution of 5, each within 1e-9, through `UnwatchedIterations`; `a search box's centred search starts at zero within plus or minus its half-width`: `(SearchBox 50.0).centredSearch 3` holds the start [0; 0; 0], the lower bounds [−50; −50; −50] and the upper [50; 50; 50]. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (`fitObservations`) and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` (`fitAbsorbingObservations`), the cheapest classes running `fitWithResidual` (step 337), show their numbers unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the scaled search lands, `ScaledSearch.solveWith` MUST hold the one bounded Levenberg–Marquardt request and `fitWithResidual` MUST call it over `SearchBox.centredSearch` with its numbers unchanged; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scaled search starts where it is told and keeps to its own box` and `a search box's centred search starts at zero within plus or minus its half-width`, the count rising by 2; unit-tests MUST pass over `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` and `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests` with their numbers unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s38 invariants MUST pass.
